fact WorkItem(id: "WI-309", description: some(value: "Load and surface operation-declaration metadata. Operation declarations already accept a [key: value] meta_block in the grammar (tree-sitter-anthill/grammar.js:319, operation_declaration) AND it is parsed into the IR (Operation.meta: Option<MetaBlock>, parse/ir.rs:336). But the loader (kb/load.rs) NEVER reads op.meta — operation metadata is silently dropped at load — and OperationInfo (stdlib/anthill/reflect/reflect.anthill:424) has no field to expose it (only name/params/return_type/effects/requires/ensures). Work: (1) loader consumes op.meta and stores it in the KB op record; (2) OperationInfo gains a meta field (or per-key surfacing) so operation metadata is queryable from reflection and the typer; (3) regression test: an operation declared with [key: value] has that metadata loaded and retrievable via OperationInfo. Motivation: proposal 046 (effect_derive / region tracking) needs [feeds: ...] metadata on operations to carry the feed-relationship for abstract/foreign higher-order operations that have no anthill body; more generally, ANY operation-level metadata (trust, source, project-defined keys) is currently parsed and thrown away. Prerequisite for 046's feeds annotation."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-16T10:44:20Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-309", author: "user", content: "Subsumed by WI-087 (operation attributes/metadata). All three work items delivered there: (1) loader consumes op.meta into the OperationInfo fact (kb/load.rs ~9119-9172, lowers meta_block -> meta(key: value, ...)); (2) OperationInfo gained a meta: Term field (reflect.anthill:474); (3) regression tests in tests/include/wi087_operation_meta_test.rs (4 tests green). Proposal-046 [feeds: ...] on body-less operations now surfaces via OperationInfo.meta for free.", at: "2026-06-16T10:44:17Z")
